<newsitem itemid="633271" id="root" date="1997-06-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sage year earnings up 25 percent.</title>
<headline>Sage year earnings up 25 percent.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>- headline diluted (cts) 132.7  vs 105.8</p>
<p>    - attrib diluted (cts)   129.3  vs 114.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    87.0   vs 70.0</p>
<p>Full name: Sage Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters had predicted EPS of 132.0, with a range 131.2-133, and a dividend of 87.0, with a range 86.0-88.0.  </p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-exceps	184.58 vs 145.36</p>
<p>    Exceptional charge	   4.44 vs 10.62 gain</p>
<p>    Pre-tax income	     180.14 vs 155.98</p>
<p>    Tax			     20.46 vs  22.94</p>
<p>    Attrib income		159.68 vs 132.89</p>
<p>    Headline earnings	  164.12 vs 122.27</p>
<p>Div payable Aug 8</p>
<p>On register July 4</p>
<p>NOTE - Exceptional charge reflects loss on discontinued operations. The company said it would offer capitalisation shares in lieu of the cash dividend.</p>
<p>Sage said consoldiated assets exceeded six billion rand and total assets under management exceeded nine billion.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
